{
  "title": "Catalog: size, count and measure words left in the item stop whole foods from resolving",
  "description": "Found while weighing whole produce and seafood by size: these lines fail as \"No supported nutrition match\" (Not recognized), not for a missing weight, because a size, piece or prep word stays in the parsed item and the resolver doesn't strip it. \"16 uncooked medium shrimp, peeled and deveined\" (item \"uncooked medium shrimp\"), \"6 black tiger shrimp (or similar large prawn)\", \"2 small kohlrabi bulbs, peeled and sliced paper thin\" (item \"kohlrabi bulbs\"), \"1 medium/small butternut squash\" (the slashed size stays in the item), \"1 crown of broccoli\", \"1 large crown broccoli\", \"3 crowns broccoli\" (the piece leads the food), \"5 roasted broccoli florets (chopped small…)\". \
Also a parse bug: \"1 medium butternut squash (peeled, seeded and sliced into 3/4\\\"\" leaves an unclosed paren in the item (\"butternut squash (peeled\"), so the note never splits off. \
And \"1 small zucchini per person for zoodles* or pho noodles\" resolves to its second alternative (pho noodles) because the first one carries \"per person for zoodles*\". \
Once these resolve, the weights are already there: shrimp sizes, kohlrabi and butternut squash medium, the broccoli crown and floret entries (curated.json / bespoke.json). \
Strip a leading or medial size word, read a slashed size (\"medium/small\") as its first size, treat \"crown(s) (of)\" and \"bulbs\" as the counted piece the way quantity.rs named_piece reads slices and leaves, and add \"uncooked\" as a leading modifier. \
Measure with make ingredient-catalog-audit (No supported nutrition match, all three corpora). \
Server-side only (ramekin-core parser and catalog), so no web or iOS change. make pipeline should produce only data/ingredient-catalog-audit.md and fixture diffs.",
